From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: take the job's IOMMU domain before it can be
 rejected

rocket_ioctl_submit_job() allocates the job with kzalloc and only assigns
rjob->domain after the task copy and both BO lookups have succeeded.
rocket_job_cleanup() puts that domain unconditionally, and every rejection
before the assignment unwinds through it -- so a malformed submit walks the
kernel into rocket_iommu_domain_put(NULL), which dereferences the NULL to
reach the kref.

Five rejection sites are reachable from an unprivileged caller, all of them
ahead of the assignment:

  task_struct_size below sizeof(struct drm_rocket_task)      -EINVAL
  an unreadable drm_rocket_job.tasks pointer                 -EFAULT
  drm_rocket_task.regcmd_count == 0                          -EINVAL
  no such in_bo handle                                       -ENOENT
  no such out_bo handle                                      -ENOENT

/dev/accel/accel0 is group `render`, so any client that may use the NPU at
all can take the machine down with one ioctl.  On an H96 MAX M9 (RK3576,
7.1.3, this series applied) [HW]:

  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1]  SMP
  pc : rocket_iommu_domain_put+0x50/0xac [rocket]
  lr : rocket_job_cleanup+0x20/0x23c [rocket]
  Call trace:
   rocket_iommu_domain_put+0x50/0xac [rocket] (P)
   rocket_job_cleanup+0x20/0x23c [rocket]
   rocket_ioctl_submit+0x3e0/0x7cc [rocket]

Take the reference at construction instead, so a rocket_job owns a domain
from the moment it exists and rocket_job_cleanup() has nothing to test.
rocket_iommu_domain_get() cannot fail -- rocket_open() creates the file's
domain before the file is usable, and it outlives every job submitted on it
-- so there is no new error path, and the reference is dropped by the same
cleanup that already ran.

Fixing the invariant at the source is preferred here over teaching
rocket_iommu_domain_put() to tolerate NULL.  The bug is an object escaping
to its destructor without its invariant established; a NULL-tolerant put
would keep every future field in that window and hide the next one.  It also
keeps this patch inside rocket_job.c, so it composes with the RK3588 series'
085 (which carries the NULL guard as a rider on the extensible-struct work)
rather than conflicting with it -- a tree that takes both gets the invariant
and the guard, and neither is wasted.

Not RK3576-specific: the code is identical in mainline and the trigger needs
no NPU-specific state, only an open DRM file.  It is carried here because
this series is what the RK3576 image applies, and that image does not take
the RK3588 series.

Verified with tests/uapi_submit_errpath_rocket in rocket-userspace, which
fires one malformed submit per site from a forked child: 0/5 sites returned
to userspace before this patch (the first killed the caller), 5/5 after.

Fixes: 0810d5ad88a1 ("accel/rocket: Add job submission IOCTL")
Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index 58848aada..c4935d1bf 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -785,6 +785,17 @@ static int rocket_ioctl_submit_job(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file
 
 	rjob->rdev = rdev;
 
+	/*
+	 * Take the IOMMU domain reference here, while the job is still empty.
+	 * rocket_job_cleanup() puts it unconditionally, and every rejection
+	 * below unwinds through there -- so acquiring it any later leaves a
+	 * window in which a malformed submit reaches the cleanup path with
+	 * job->domain still NULL from the kzalloc.  The get cannot fail: the
+	 * file's domain is created in rocket_open() and outlives every job
+	 * submitted on it.
+	 */
+	rjob->domain = rocket_iommu_domain_get(file_priv);
+
 	ret = drm_sched_job_init(&rjob->base,
 				 &file_priv->sched_entity,
 				 1, NULL, file->client_id);
@@ -809,8 +820,6 @@ static int rocket_ioctl_submit_job(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file
 
 	rjob->out_bo_count = job->out_bo_handle_count;
 
-	rjob->domain = rocket_iommu_domain_get(file_priv);
-
 	ret = rocket_job_push(rjob);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_cleanup_job;
-- 
